QuestGuidance.Register("en",295,{
[9409]="70041D79\n1\tDefeat Okurayo the Minstrel quickly\tDefeat Okurayo the Minstrel quickly, before he heartens our foes and dispirits our men. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[9410]="700428C9\n1\tDefeat Okurayo the Minstrel quickly\tDefeat Okurayo the Minstrel quickly, before he heartens our foes and dispirits our men. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[9411]="70062E54\n1\tSearch for Ol' Gil\tSioned has asked you to look for her father, a hobbit affectionately known as Ol' Tipsy Gil. Gil can be found around Glyn Helyg.\n2\tContinue searching for Gil\tYou found an empty wine bottle, so Tipsy Gil may be close by! Keep searching for him in Glyn Helyg.\n3\tFill the wine bottle\tYou managed to find Gil, but he's too drunk to make it home for dinner. He has asked you to bring him some water to help him sober up. You should fill the wine bottle you found with water from the nearby fountain.\n4\tBring the water to Gil\tWith a full bottle of fresh water in hand, you are ready to help sober up Ol' Tipsy Gil. Gil is in Glyn Helyg.\n5\tTalk to Sioned\tYou should let Sioned know that her father is on the way to recovery and will be around for dinner soon. Sioned is in Glyn Helyg.\n",
[9412]="700449E9\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Acquaintance of the Defenders of Minas Tirith.\n",
[9413]="700449E7\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered a Friend of the Defenders of Minas Tirith.\n",
[9414]="700449E8\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered an Ally of the Defenders of Minas Tirith.\n",
[9415]="700449E6\n1\tTalk to Ransroth\tBy completing this quest, you will be considered Kindred to the Defenders of Minas Tirith.\n",
[9416]="7000799F\n1\tBring Sally's chain to Old Bauman\030Collect Sally's chain\tOld Bauman's farm lies far to the east of Combe, beyond the brigand camps in the Chetwood, at the end of the eastward path. Old Bauman is at the logging camp, south of the Chetwood, east of Combe. Old Bauman lost his farm to the Blackwolds when they retreated from Archet, and he would like you to go there and retrieve his Sally's chain for him.\n",
[9417]="70003711\n1\tDefeat Old Bloodtusk\tOld Bloodtusk's den, which is built in a rotten, old tree stump, lies east of Sprigley's Farm. Cal Sprigley has asked you to dispose of Old Bloodtusk before the boar can bring harm to anyone else.\n2\tTalk to Cal Sprigley at his farm\tCal Sprigley awaits your return. At Cal Sprigley's request, you hunted and slew the great boar Old Bloodtusk. You should return to the farmer with news of your success.\n",
[9418]="7000324E\n1\tDefeat wights to find a trophy for Nithi\tThe mounds of the old Edain are a distance to the north-east of Gondamon. Nithi asked you to journey to the old Edain barrows and collect a trophy to prove to Galti that there are wights amid the old mounds.\n2\tBring your trophy back to Nithi\tNithi can be found in some Elf-ruins to the west of Haudh Lin in Ered Luin. Nithi asked you to journey to the old Edain barrows and collect a trophy to prove to Galti that there are wights amid the old mounds.\n",
[9419]="700005BF\n1\tFind Doderic Brandybuck\tDoderic Brandybuck may be at Bald Hill in the Old Forest, east of the Bonfire Glade. Maggot's Farmhand sent you to Brandy Hall to look for Farmer Maggot's son Rollo. Saradoc Brandybuck has suggested that his nephew Doderic may have taken Rollo out to the Old Forest.\n2\tFind Rollo Maggot\tRollo Maggot may be found at an abandoned cottage near the Withywindle, south-east of Bald Hill. It is reached by heading west through the Shifting Wood, then turning south and south-east. Doderic Brandybuck is worried about his friend Rollo Maggot, who chased after a brigand into the Forest.\n3\tTalk to Doderic Brandybuck at Bald Hill\tDoderic Brandybuck is waiting at Bald Hill to the north of the cottage, east of the Bonfire Glade. You found Rollo Maggot standing over the corpse of a Man. He asked you to return to Doderic Brandybuck and tell him that he is all right, and there is no need to worry. He also asked you not to tell Doderic what happened with the brigand.\n4\tCelandine can be found on the border of Newbury and Crickhollow in the northern part of Buckland. You found Rollo Maggot standing in shock over the corpse of a brigand, but he seemed unharmed. He asked that you show his notes to Doderic, and Doderic suggested that you bring them to his cousin Celandine.\t\n5\tTalk to Wilmac Brandybuck in Newbury\tWilmac Brandybuck is just inside the Hay Gate in Newbury, the northern section of Buckland. Wilmac Brandybuck still knows nothing of Rollo's whereabouts. You should speak with him to put his mind at ease.\n",
[9420]="700005C0\n1\tTalk to Farmer Maggot at Bamfurlong\tBamfurlong is south on the river road, on the western side of the Brandywine Bridge. Celandine Brandybuck has asked you to enquire about notes she requested from Farmer Maggot at his farm, Bamfurlong, on her behalf.\n2\tTalk to Rollo Maggot, Doderic Brandybuck, or Wilmac Brandybuck in Newbury\tRollo Maggot, Doderic Brandybuck, or Wilmac Brandybuck are in the area of Newbury just inside the Hay Gate in Buckland Farmer Maggot sent you to find Rollo Maggot, Doderic Brandybuck, or Wilmac Brandybuck to retrieve his notes.\n",
[9421]="70008B87\n1\tTalk to Gonediad\tGonediad is somewhere in Rivendell. Sigrun has expressed his doubts about the gifting of Mírdanant to Durin by the Elves of Eregion, but has decided such old enmities must be cast aside if the new evils lurking within Helegrod are to be defeated. He has asked you to speak with Gonediad, learned in the lore of Eregion, about the return of the dragon Thorog.\n",
[9422]="70047BE7\n1\tTalk to Faramir, son of Ondoher outside Ondoher's Folly\tFaramir can be found outside Ondoher's Folly. Faramir has asked to tell you the tale of the Wainriders in the Wastes. You should speak to him when you are ready to hear it.\n2\tTalk to Artamir outside Ondoher's Folly\tArtamir can be found outside Ondoher's Folly. You have heard Faramir's tale of the Wainriders and should now speak to Artamir.\n",
[9423]="70000DAD\n1\tSearch Old Odo's farmstead\tOdo Burrow's old leaf-farm is south of the clearing where you found the missing waggon. When you found Longo's missing waggon, there was no sign of Gerebert Took, but the leaf had been moved southwards. Rollo Boffin suggested you search boxes and crates at Odo Burrow's old farm for some sign of Gerebert. He warned you to bring friends, for it might be dangerous.\n2\tTalk to Esilia Took\tEsilia Took can be found near the centre of Tuckborough. At old Odo's leaf-barn, you stumbled across Gerebert Took. Once you freed him, you were attacked by some strange Men. After defending Gerebert from the Men who attacked you, he escaped and said he would meet you back at Esilia Took's house.\n",
[9424]="70035759\n1\tExamine the strange ice-floe into Finglas' mead\tThe ice-floe can be found at the western end of Finglas' mead. Mossbeard has asked you to examine the unnatural ice-floe in Finglas' Mead.\n2\tLook at the fallen branches\030Find a higher vantage point near the frozen waterfall in Finglas' mead\tThe branches are above on a raised section of the hill. Perhaps you can look from atop the hill on the left side of the ice-floe. Mossbeard wants you to look at the branches atop the hill to the right of the ice-floe in Finglas' Mead. He fears they may belong to the elder Huorn of which he spoke.\n3\tSearch for some sign of the elder Huorn\tThe younger Huorn can be found on the hillside in north-west Balewood. Mossbeard wants you to search on the hillside for a sign of the Huorn. He hopes that the elder Huorn has escaped a foul fate.\n4\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard is at your side. Your search has come to an end. Mossbeard is deeply saddened by the loss of life in the forest. You should speak to him.\n",
[9425]="70000D4E\n1\tFind Old Sally\tBelco Brockhouse's pig, Old Sally, may be found near the big willow south-east of Belco's farm. Belco has asked you to find his pig, Old Sally, and bring her back to his barn. He warned you that she spooks easily, and if she gets too scared, she may run away.\n2\tTalk to Belco Brockhouse\tBelco Brockhouse can be found south of the Tuckborough town centre. You should speak with Belco Brockhouse and let him know that you led his pig, Old Sally, back to his barn.\n",
[9426]="700571C3\n1\tTalk to Náth in Limlók\tNáth cam be found in Limlók. You should talk to Náth.\n2\tCross the Skerabrygg in the Floodfells\tSkerabrygg can be found in the Floodfells. You should cross the Skerabrygg.\n3\tContinue to Sundergrót\tSundergrót can be found in the Floodfells. You should travel to Sundergrót.\n4\tTalk to Náth outside of Sundergrót\tSundergrót can be found in the Floodfells. You should talk to Náth outside of Sundergrót.\n5\tScout Egvárth\tEgvárth can be found in the Floodfells. You should scout Egvárth.\n6\tDefeat foes at Egvárth (total: 8)\030Destroy weapons at Egvárth (total: 6)\tEgvárth can be found in the Floodfells. You should clear Egvárth of foes.\n7\tScout Stramvárth\tStramvárth can be found in the Floodfells. You should scout Stramvárth.\n8\tDefeat foes at Stramvárth (total: 10)\030Destroy supplies at Stramvárth (total: 6)\tStramvárth can be found in the Floodfells. You should clear Stramvárth of foes.\n9\tTalk to Rúzat outside of Sundergrót\tSundergrót can be found in the Floodfells. You should talk to Rúzat outside of Sundergrót.\n10\tComplete the quest \"Sundergrót: The Intruders\"\030Complete the quest \"Sundergrót: Goblin Supplies\"\030Complete the quest \"Sundergrót: Evaluating the Hold\"\030Complete the quest \"Sundergrót: Mining Sappers\"\030Complete the quest \"Sundergrót: Biting Insects\"\tSundergrót can be found in the Floodfells. You should survey Sundergrót's interior.\n11\tTalk to Rúzat outside of Sundergrót\tSundergrót can be found in the Floodfells. You should talk to Rúzat outside of Sundergrót.\n",
[9427]="7000383B\n1\tSearch the ruins to the north-west for treasure\tThere are some ruins to the north-west. There may be something of value to be found within them.\n2\tSearch the ruins to the north-west for treasure\tThere are ruins in the distance to the north-west that may contain treasures of great value.\n3\tBring damaged dwarf-chest to Larus Sharpshard\030Collect Damaged Dwarf-chest\tAn old dwarf strongbox catches your eye. Word is, Larus Sharpshard is looking for a specific treasure and this may be the one he seeks. Larus Sharpshard is located in a camp just north of High Crag.\n",
[9428]="70052E8F\n1\tChildren of the Woodmen can be found in Hultvís. Unwilling to speak more of it himself, Atta has told you to ask the children of Hultvís about a creature named Ubb.\t\n2\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. You have spoken to the children of Hultvís about Ubb, and you have learned much of the legend of the Snatcher. You should return to Atta.\n",
[9429]="7002C7D1\n1\tBring the antlers of Oldheart to Ninil\tNinil is in Haldirith. You should bring the antlers of Oldheart to Ninil.\n",
[9430]="70059D85\n1\tComplete missions (total: 45)\tMissions can be completed across Middle-earth. You should complete missions.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have completed many missions across Middle-earth.\n",
