[9434]="70044116\n1\tDefend soldiers of Minas Tirith from fell spirits and the Enemy's fell beast\tYou should defeat the fell spirits threatening the remaining warriors of Gondor, and drive off the Enemy's vile fell beasts.\n",
[9435]="700447FA\n1\tDefend soldiers of Minas Tirith from fell spirits and the Enemy's fell beast\tYou should defeat the fell spirits threatening the remaining warriors of Gondor, and drive off the Enemy's vile fell beasts.\n",
[9436]="7004309B\n1\tTalk to Luntil the boatwoman\tLuntil, the boatwoman, can be found in a marshy inlet south along the shores of the Anduin in Lossarnach. You should find Luntil and greet her in Dindal's name. She will take you across the river to find Lord Faramir's Rangers.\n",
[9437]="7003557B\n1\tDefeat Orc Scouts near Alferth's memorial (total: 4)\tWhite Hand Orc-riders roam too near Alferth's memorial, and must be driven off. You should defeat Orcs near Alferth's memorial.\n2\tCompleted\tThe White Hand enemies have been driven away from the site of Alferth's memorial.\n",
[9438]="700300FB\n1\tEnter Harwick at your own risk while on notice\tYou have been flagged by Captain Agelmund as a trespasser in Harwick. If you venture into that city, beware the guards -- for you are on notice, and they will banish you on sight. To earn Harding's favour, you must assist Captain Agelmund, Sergeant Hubyrt, and Cíllan. Only they can help you gain your welcome to Harwick.\n2\tSpeak with Thane Harding\tThane Harding is in the Mead Hall of Harwick. You should speak with the Thane, now that you are no longer on notice.\n",
[9439]="70031825\n1\tTalk to Winsig\tWinsig can be found in the mead hall of Walstow. Winsig fears that some great evil is about to descend upon Snowbourn after distracting the folk of Walstow with a smaller attack. She wishes to ride to Snowbourn with you and confront the vile sorceror, Crúmgam.\n2\tTalk to Gísil in Snowbourn\tGísil can be found outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn. In the aftermath of the battle, Crúmgam has been defeated and the Orc-force broken. Peace has returned to the Sutcrofts.\n",
[9440]="700230DD\n1\tTalk to someone whom Bilbo trusted with a special and secret gift\tDeliver the letter to someone whom Bilbo would have trusted with an important secret. They will likely be very near the festival grounds, perhaps even part of the festival. The writ speaks of a trustworthy sort with whom Bilbo struck a deal before he left the Shire. Apparently, there is a reward to be delivered to anyone not related to the Sackville-Bagginses.\n",
